## Project Architecture

### Language: Pure C++ (No Blueprints)
- All gameplay logic must be in C++ (.cpp/.h files)
- Only use Blueprints for:
  - UI widgets (UMG)
  - Material instances
  - Actor placement in levels
  - Visual scripting where explicitly requested

### Code Organization:
```
Source/MechInterior/
├── PlayerMechPawn.cpp/.h           - Main player mech
├── EnemyMechPawn.cpp/.h            - AI enemy mechs
├── MechMovementComponent.cpp/.h    - Locomotion system
├── ReactorSystemComponent.cpp/.h   - Heat/power management
├── WeaponSystemComponent.cpp/.h    - Weapon systems
├── DamageManagementComponent.cpp/.h - Hull integrity
├── MechStation.cpp/.h              - Station control (pilot/gunner/tech)
├── FireHazardActor.cpp/.h          - Interior hazards
├── CoolantLeakActor.cpp/.h         - Interior hazards
├── ElectricalArcActor.cpp/.h       - Interior hazards
├── ProceduralMechGeometry.cpp/.h   - Mech visual generation
├── ProceduralInteriorGeometry.cpp/.h - Cockpit generation
├── TerrainSpawner.cpp/.h           - Environment generation
└── MechGameMode.cpp/.h             - Game mode
```

---

## Code Style

### Naming Conventions:
- Classes: `APlayerMechPawn`, `UMechMovementComponent`
- Functions: `PascalCase` - `FireWeapon()`, `GetHeatPercentage()`
- Variables: `camelCase` - `currentTarget`, `bIsOccupied`
- Member variables: Prefix with type - `bIsMoving`, `CurrentHeat`, `TargetLocation`
- Constants: `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` or `kConstantName`

### Unreal Prefixes:
- `A` - Actor classes (APawn, AActor)
- `U` - UObject/Component classes (UActorComponent, USceneComponent)
- `F` - Structs (FVector, FRotator)
- `E` - Enums (EStationType, EDamageType)
- `I` - Interfaces (IInteractable)
- `T` - Templates (TArray, TMap)

### UCLASS/UPROPERTY Requirements:
- All gameplay classes must use `UCLASS()`
- Properties exposed to editor/Blueprint: `UPROPERTY(EditAnywhere, BlueprintReadWrite, Category = "...")`
- Properties visible in editor: `UPROPERTY(VisibleAnywhere, BlueprintReadOnly, Category = "...")`
- Replicated properties: Add `Replicated` and implement `GetLifetimeReplicatedProps()`

---

## Network Replication

### Multiplayer is Required:
- All gameplay-critical properties must replicate
- Use `DOREPLIFETIME(ClassName, PropertyName)` in `GetLifetimeReplicatedProps()`
- Mark functions that run on server: `UFUNCTION(Server, Reliable)`
- Mark functions that run on clients: `UFUNCTION(Client, Reliable)`
- Authority checks: Use `HasAuthority()` before modifying replicated state

### Example:
```cpp
UPROPERTY(Replicated, BlueprintReadOnly, Category = "State")
float CurrentHeat;

void APlayerMechPawn::GetLifetimeReplicatedProps(TArray<FLifetimeProperty>& OutLifetimeProps) const
{
    Super::GetLifetimeReplicatedProps(OutLifetimeProps);
    DOREPLIFETIME(APlayerMechPawn, CurrentHeat);
}
```

---

## Component System

### Use Components for Modular Systems:
- Movement → `UMechMovementComponent`
- Reactor → `UReactorSystemComponent`
- Weapons → `UWeaponSystemComponent`
- Damage → `UDamageManagementComponent`

### Component Creation:
```cpp
// In Constructor
MechMovement = CreateDefaultSubobject<UMechMovementComponent>(TEXT("MechMovement"));

// Don't call SetupAttachment on UActorComponent (only USceneComponent)
```

---

## Station Control System

### Possession-Based Control:
When a player uses a station (Pilot, Gunner, Technician):
1. Store original pawn reference
2. `PlayerController->Possess(TargetPawn)`
3. Input now routes to possessed pawn
4. On exit: `PlayerController->Possess(OriginalPawn)`

### Example:
```cpp
void AMechStation::UseStation(APawn* User)
{
    APlayerController* PC = Cast<APlayerController>(User->GetController());
    OriginalPawn = User;
    StationController = PC;

    if (StationType == EStationType::Pilot && OwningMech)
    {
        PC->Possess(OwningMech);  // WASD now controls mech
    }
}
```

---

## Input Binding

### Setup Input in C++:
```cpp
void APlayerMechPawn::SetupPlayerInputComponent(UInputComponent* PlayerInputComponent)
{
    Super::SetupPlayerInputComponent(PlayerInputComponent);

    PlayerInputComponent->BindAxis("MoveForward", this, &APlayerMechPawn::InputMoveForward);
    PlayerInputComponent->BindAxis("MoveRight", this, &APlayerMechPawn::InputMoveRight);
    PlayerInputComponent->BindAction("Fire", IE_Pressed, this, &APlayerMechPawn::InputFireWeapon);
}
```

### Input Axis Names (DefaultInput.ini):
- MoveForward, MoveRight, Turn, LookUp
- Fire, Brace, Boost
- Use, Interact

---

## AI System

### Enemy AI State Machine:
```
Idle → Patrol → Alert → Engage → Retreat → Disabled
```

### AI Implementation Rules:
- Use timer-based scanning (1 Hz, not every tick)
- Line-of-sight checks with `LineTraceSingleByChannel`
- Range management (optimal combat range: 1km)
- State transitions based on: target presence, health, distance
- Do NOT use navigation mesh (mech movement is custom physics)

---

## Damage System

### Section-Based Damage:
- 6 mech sections: Head, Torso, LeftArm, RightArm, LeftLeg, RightLeg
- Convert world hit location to section using local transform
- Apply damage to specific section integrity
- 30% chance to spawn interior hazard on damage

### Damage Types:
```cpp
enum class EDamageType : uint8
{
    Ballistic,   // Physical projectiles
    Energy,      // Lasers, plasma
    Explosive,   // Missiles
    Melee,       // Close combat
    Environmental // Falls, collisions
};
```

---

## Hazard System

### 3 Hazard Types:
1. **FireHazardActor** - Spreads over time, damages nearby players, extinguishable
2. **CoolantLeakActor** - Area damage, repairable
3. **ElectricalArcActor** - Periodic shocks, repairable

### Hazard Spawning:
```cpp
// Spawn at damage location inside mech
FVector SpawnLocation = GetInteriorLocationFromWorldHit(HitLocation);
GetWorld()->SpawnActor<AFireHazardActor>(AFireHazardActor::StaticClass(), SpawnLocation, FRotator::ZeroRotator);
```

